insert into public.content_snippets (key, body) values
('example_health_2', 'At 60 I weigh 84 kg, down from 102, and I have kept it off for three years. I lift three mornings a week and walk every day. My blood pressure is normal without medication. I sleep seven hours and wake before the alarm. My doctor uses the word excellent, and I no longer dread the appointment.'),
('example_health_3', 'At 63 I can get down on the floor with my grandchildren and get back up without thinking about it. My knees and back are strong because I do the boring work: mobility every morning, strength twice a week, a long walk on Sundays. I have energy at four in the afternoon. I drink rarely and I never miss it.'),
('example_health_4', 'At 58 I finish my first half marathon, and it is not the last. I run four days a week and I love it. My resting heart rate is in the fifties. I eat real food, mostly cooked at home. I have the same waist size I had at thirty-five, and my clothes fit the way I want them to.'),
('example_health_5', 'At 65 I am the fittest man in my family, in any generation. I swim three mornings a week and lift twice. My shoulders are back and my chest is open. I have not smoked in six years. I take the stairs without a second thought and I can carry my own bags anywhere in the world.'),
('example_health_6', 'At 61 I have reversed the warning my doctor gave me at 56. My blood sugar is in the normal range. I weigh 88 kg and most of what I lost was around my middle. I walk ten thousand steps a day, lift weights on Monday, Wednesday and Friday, and I am in bed by ten.'),
('example_health_7', 'At 59 I move without pain for the first time in fifteen years. The shoulder is strong, the back is quiet. I train with a coach twice a week and stretch every evening. I play eighteen holes and walk the course. I look in the mirror and see a man who takes care of himself.'),
('example_health_8', 'At 67 I hike for five days in the mountains with men twenty years younger and keep up. I train for it all year: hills, legs, core, long days on my feet. I weigh 79 kg. I sleep deeply. My body is something I use and enjoy, not something I manage and apologise for.'),
('example_health_9', 'At 62 I am strong. I can deadlift my own bodyweight and hang from a bar for a minute. I eat enough protein, I see the sun before I see a screen, and I am asleep by half past nine. My energy is steady all day. People guess I am ten years younger, and I feel it.'),
('example_health_10', 'At 64 I ride my bike eighty kilometres on a Saturday and feel good on Sunday. I gave up the nightly wine three years ago and my sleep changed overnight. I weigh 81 kg, my waist is 86 cm, and I have a check-up every year that I look forward to. Fitness is just part of who I am.'),
('example_purpose_2', 'I run a business that works without me in the room. A general manager handles the week. I spend my time on the three clients I enjoy most and on training the next generation. I work four days. The business pays me well and would be worth buying, though I am in no hurry to sell.'),
('example_purpose_3', 'I have left the corporate job and built a consulting practice around what I know best. Six good clients, no more. I choose who I work with and I say no often. I earn as much as I did before in half the hours, and for the first time in decades my work feels like mine.'),
('example_purpose_4', 'I teach what I spent thirty years learning. I mentor younger tradesmen and run a small training course twice a year. My own business has two crews and a waiting list. I am off the tools except when I want to be. My name means quality in this town, and that matters more to me than the money.'),
('example_purpose_5', 'I still work at the firm, but on my terms. I lead one team, I mentor four people, and I leave at five. I am the person others come to when the problem is hard. My finances are in order: the house is paid off, the retirement fund is on track, and money no longer keeps me awake.'),
('example_purpose_6', 'I have written the book I talked about for twenty years, and a second is under way. I speak a dozen times a year to rooms that want to hear it. Income comes from the books, the talks and a small group I coach. I wake up knowing what my work is for.'),
('example_purpose_7', 'I am retired from full-time work and busier with things that matter. I sit on two boards, I volunteer with a men''s group every week, and I help three young founders for nothing. Our investments pay for the life we want. I am useful, and I know it.'),
('example_purpose_8', 'I sold the company and did not disappear. I invest in a few small businesses and help their owners avoid the mistakes I made. I work about twenty hours a week, from anywhere. I have enough, I know what enough is, and I give some of it away on purpose.'),
('example_purpose_9', 'I have changed careers at 57 and it was the right call. I do work that uses my hands and my head, and I am good at it. I earn less than I once did and need less than I once thought. The debts are gone. On Sunday night I look forward to Monday.'),
('example_purpose_10', 'I own three rental properties and a small online business that pays the bills between them. I spend my mornings building, my afternoons free. I have taught my children how money works. I am not rich by anyone else''s measure, but I am free, and every month I am a little more so.'),
('example_relationships_2', 'My wife and I have found each other again. We walk together most mornings, we have one night a week that is ours, and we talk about more than logistics. My daughter rings me for advice and my son asks me to come fishing. Sunday lunch at our place is something people do not want to miss.'),
('example_relationships_3', 'I have repaired things with my son. It took an apology and two years of showing up, and now we speak every week. I see my grandchildren often and they run to the door. My partner tells her friends I am the most present man she knows, and she means it.'),
('example_relationships_4', 'I am single and I am not lonely. I have four close friends I see every month and can ring at any hour. My children and I have dinner every fortnight. I am open to meeting someone, and I will bring a full life to it rather than an empty one.'),
('example_relationships_5', 'My wife trusts me completely, and I have earned it. We travel twice a year, just the two of us. I put the phone away at dinner. My brother and I are close again after years of distance. When someone in my family is in trouble, I am the first person they call.'),
('example_relationships_6', 'After the divorce I rebuilt, slowly and properly. My kids stay with me because they want to, and their friends are welcome too. I am on good terms with their mother. I have a partner who makes me laugh, and a group of mates I ride with every Saturday.'),
('example_relationships_7', 'I am the father I wish I had. I know what is going on in my children''s lives because they tell me. I visit my mother every week and I listen more than I talk. My wife and I still hold hands. I have friends I have known for forty years and I look after those friendships.'),
('example_relationships_8', 'Since my wife died I have learned to let people in. My daughters and I talk most days. I have dinner with friends twice a week and I host as often as I am hosted. I have made room for new love without guilt. The people in my life know exactly what they mean to me because I tell them.'),
('example_relationships_9', 'My partner and I are a team. We plan our year together, we argue well, and we make up quickly. My stepchildren treat me as family. I have two friends I would trust with anything and I see them every week. I remember birthdays, I make the call, and I turn up.'),
('example_relationships_10', 'My grandchildren know me well, not just my name. I take each of them out on their own once a month. My wife and I have a standing date on Fridays. My sons ask what I think, and sometimes they even do it. Our house is noisy at Christmas and that is exactly how I want it.'),
('example_lifestyle_2', 'A house with a garden ten minutes from the beach, paid off. Coffee on the deck at sunrise. Two overseas trips a year and a long weekend away every couple of months. A good gym nearby. Dinner out with friends on Fridays. Enough money that I do not check the price of things that matter.'),
('example_lifestyle_3', 'A small farm an hour from the city, with a workshop, a vegetable garden and room for the grandchildren to run. A city apartment for when we need it. One big trip a year, somewhere neither of us has been. Good boots, a good ute, a good dog. Space, quiet and time.'),
('example_lifestyle_4', 'An apartment in the city, walking distance to everything: the gym, the market, the theatre, good coffee. No car most days. A month in Europe each year, living like a local in one place. Clothes that fit well. A calendar with white space in it.'),
('example_lifestyle_5', 'A home on the water with a boat at the jetty. Fishing at dawn twice a week. Friends over for dinner most weekends. Winters somewhere warm for six weeks. A study full of books and a comfortable chair. Nothing flashy, everything well made.'),
('example_lifestyle_6', 'A caravan and no fixed plan for four months of the year, seeing the country properly. A simple, comfortable home base near the family for the rest. Golf on Wednesdays. A weekly lunch with old mates. Low costs, no debts, and the freedom to say yes at short notice.'),
('example_lifestyle_7', 'A house in the hills with a view and a fireplace. A home gym and a sauna. Skiing every winter, somewhere warm every spring. A table that seats twelve and gets used. Work from the study three mornings a week, and the rest of the time is ours.'),
('example_lifestyle_8', 'A townhouse close to the grandchildren, so I can do school pick-up twice a week. A club where I swim, train and see friends. A fortnight at the same beach house every January with the whole family. One special trip a year with my wife. Time is the luxury, and I have it.'),
('example_lifestyle_9', 'A place by the sea in a small town where people know my name. Morning swim, late breakfast, a few hours of work I enjoy. A motorbike in the garage and a long ride once a month. A trip to Japan or Italy every year. A simple wardrobe of things I love wearing.'),
('example_lifestyle_10', 'Two homes: one near the children, one somewhere warm for the winter. Business class when the flight is long. A trainer twice a week and a massage once a fortnight. Season tickets to the football. Generous with family, careful with everything else. Comfort without clutter.'),
('example_moment_2', 'I am standing at the finish line of a half marathon, hands on my knees, laughing. My wife is at the barrier with our grandchildren and they are shouting my name. Five years ago I could not run to the corner. I did not get lucky. I got up every morning and did the work.'),
('example_moment_3', 'I am at the head of a long table in our garden at Christmas. All of my children are here, with their partners and their children. Someone is telling a story about me and everyone is laughing. My wife catches my eye across the table. I built this, and I nearly did not.'),
('example_moment_4', 'I am on the deck at sunrise with a coffee, and the house behind me is quiet. Nothing hurts. Nothing is owed. There is no email I am dreading. In an hour I will train, and after that the day is mine. I feel calm all the way through, and I earned it.'),
('example_moment_5', 'I am walking my daughter down the aisle. She squeezes my arm and says she is glad I am here, and I know she means all of it, the last five years as much as today. I am fit, I am clear-eyed, and I am completely present. I would not swap places with anyone.'),
('example_moment_6', 'I am on a summit with my son after four days of walking. We are sitting on a rock, sharing a bar of chocolate, not saying much. The view goes on forever. He says, I did not think you would still be able to do this. I smile, because I knew I would.'),
('example_moment_7', 'I am handing the keys to my general manager for the last time as the boss. The business is strong, the team is good, and my work here is finished well. I walk out to the car park, where my wife is waiting with the bags already in the boot. We have a plane to catch.'),
('example_moment_8', 'I am in a small room with twelve men who have just finished the programme I built. One of them stands up and says his wife has her husband back. Another says his doctor cannot believe the numbers. I think of where I started, and I know my hard years were not wasted.'),
('example_moment_9', 'I am on a boat, early, with my oldest friend. The water is flat and the lines are in. We have been coming here for forty years, and for a while I stopped. I look at him and think: I kept this. I kept all the things that matter. I am healthy, I am free, and I am not in a hurry.'),
('example_moment_10', 'I am sitting in my doctor''s office and she turns the screen around to show me the results. Everything is where it should be. She says, whatever you are doing, keep doing it. I walk out into the sun, ring my wife, and tell her we are going to have a very long time together.')
